/**
  \defgroup MitkPlanarFigureModule PlanarFigure
  \ingroup MITKModules

  \brief Planar figure data types.

  A planar figure, see mitk::PlanarFigure, is a geometric figure on a plane,
  for example a line, a circle or a polygon, that measures what it covers.
  It is defined by its control points in the 2D coordinates of its plane;
  contours, decorations, handles and measurements are computed from them.
  mitk::CreatePlanarFigure() creates a figure of a type given by its
  identifier, such as "four_point_angle".

  Figures are saved as JSON files with the extension .pf.json. Files of the
  previous XML format with the extension .pf are still read.

  mitk::PlanarFigureInteractor places and edits figures in 2D render windows,
  mitk::PlanarFigureVtkMapper2D draws them, see \ref PlanarPropertiesPage.
*/
